{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "GoStudy — How My App Works",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "src/App.tsx",
      "line": 89,
      "title": "🚪 First Launch Logic",
      "description": "This function (LandingRoute) decides what users see when they open the app:\n\n- Brand new user (no data) → goes to onboarding wizard\n- Returning user (has data) → goes straight to Home\n\nThis is why the welcome/setup page only shows once."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/App.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🗺️ START HERE — The App Map",
      "description": "This is App.tsx — the brain of the whole app. Every screen (page) is registered here as a Route. If you want to know what screens exist and what URL they live at, this is the file to check.\n\nThink of it like a table of contents for all your pages."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/WelcomePage.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "👋 Welcome Page",
      "description": "The first screen new users see. Has two options:\n- 'Continue as Guest' → uses app without account, saves data locally only\n- 'Sign In' → opens Google/Apple login\n\nGuest mode sets a flag called 'guest_mode' in localStorage."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/Index.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🎓 Onboarding Wizard (5 steps)",
      "description": "This is the setup wizard new users go through:\n1. Enter your name\n2. Choose grading system (APC, French, or Nigerian University)\n3. Pick your class level\n4. Set your target grade\n5. Choose your subjects\n\nWhen finished, it saves everything to localStorage and sends you to Home."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/Home.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🏠 Home Screen — The Main Dashboard",
      "description": "This is the most important page in the app. It shows:\n- Your current average vs your target\n- Each subject with its grade and status (on track / at risk)\n- Your daily streak counter\n- Notification bell\n- Quick buttons to add new marks\n\nThis file is very long because it does a lot. Don't be intimidated — each section is clearly separated."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/exam-logic.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🧮 The Grade Calculator",
      "description": "This is the math engine. Every grade calculation in the app runs through here:\n- Subject average calculation\n- Overall yearly average\n- 'What do I need to score next?' calculations\n- Best/worst possible final grade\n\nIf grades are showing wrong, this is where to look."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/storage.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "💾 Where All Data Lives",
      "description": "This file controls saving and loading ALL user data.\n\n- loadState() → reads your subjects, grades, settings from localStorage\n- saveState() → writes it back and queues a cloud sync\n\nKey: all data is stored under the key 'scoretarget_state' in localStorage. This is your app's database on the device."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🔐 Login & Sync System",
      "description": "Manages whether the user is logged in. Key behaviors:\n- Checks for existing session on startup (times out after 600ms so app never hangs)\n- On login: pulls cloud data down (or uploads local data up)\n- On logout: wipes local data to protect privacy\n- Syncs data to cloud every 30 seconds in the background\n\nProvides 'user' and 'session' to the whole app."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/contexts/AppConfigContext.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "💎 Premium / Paywall System",
      "description": "Controls who can access premium features. Key functions:\n- requirePremium(action) → runs the action if premium, shows paywall if not\n- openPremiumGate() → directly shows the 'enter your code' popup\n- openDownloadLimitGate() → shows 'you hit 5/month limit' popup\n\nUse the usePremium() hook in any page to check if user is premium."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/config/app-features.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "⚙️ Feature Toggles (Master Control)",
      "description": "This is the control panel for the whole app.\n\nKey settings:\n- PREMIUM_ENABLED: false → production mode, quota system active\n- FREE_DOWNLOAD_LIMIT: 5 → free users get 5 downloads/month\n- DEBUG_MODE: false → set to true for extra console logs\n\n⚠️ WARNING: Setting PREMIUM_ENABLED: true gives everyone free premium. Only do this for testing!"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/services/downloadService.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "📥 Download System",
      "description": "Handles everything about saving PDFs to the device:\n- Downloads papers and books\n- Tracks download progress\n- Checks your monthly quota (5 free/month)\n- Verifies file integrity after download\n- Lets you delete and share files\n\nThis is the most complex service in the app."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/services/subscriptionService.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🎟️ Subscription Codes (Not a Payment System!)",
      "description": "GoStudy uses CODE-based premium — users buy or receive a code and enter it in the app. There's no credit card processing.\n\nThis service:\n- Validates codes against the Supabase database\n- Stores subscription status locally\n- Tracks expiry dates\n- Knows which subjects are unlocked for subject packs"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/i18n.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🌍 All App Text (English + French)",
      "description": "Every single text string shown in the app lives here as a key-value pair.\n\nFormat:\n  en: { key: 'English text' }\n  fr: { key: 'French text' }\n\nIf you need to change any label, button, or message in the app — this is the file. Use Ctrl+F to find the text you want to change."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/Simulator.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🎯 What-If Simulator",
      "description": "The grade simulator page. Shows sliders for each mark type across all subjects. As you drag, it recalculates your projected final average in real time.\n\n'What would my average be if I scored 80 on the next test?' — this answers that.\n\nSaving a strategy is premium-only."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/LibraryDirect.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "📚 Past Papers Library",
      "description": "The exam papers library. Fetches papers from Supabase (the cloud database). Users can:\n- Filter by subject, year, class level\n- Download PDFs (up to 5/month free)\n- View papers in-app\n\nWhen a user hits 5 downloads, the quota gate popup appears automatically."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/MyDownloads.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "📂 My Downloads",
      "description": "Shows all PDFs saved on this device. Users can:\n- Open, share, or delete individual files\n- See file sizes and download dates\n- View their quota usage (e.g. '3 of 5 used this month')\n\nAlso shows 'cloud-only' downloads — files marked as downloaded in the cloud but not present on this specific device."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/Profile.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "👤 Profile & Academic Data",
      "description": "Where users manage their academic setup:\n- Edit name, class, and target grade\n- Add/remove subjects (free users limited to 5)\n- View grade history by semester\n- For Nigerian university students: add semesters, view GPA and CGPA\n- Archive old semesters to start fresh"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/contexts/ThemeContext.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🎨 Themes & Accent Colors",
      "description": "Controls the visual look of the app:\n- Themes: light, dark, midnight, ink, system\n- Accent colors: Amber, Blue, Teal, Magenta, Cyan, Purple\n\nApplies these as CSS variables to the HTML root so every component automatically picks up the right colors. Accent color syncs to cloud so it follows users between devices."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/services/hybridSyncService.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "☁️ Cloud Sync Logic",
      "description": "The smart sync layer that decides what happens when local data and cloud data might conflict:\n\n- Cloud has onboarding data? → Pull it down (cloud wins)\n- Local has onboarding data (guest mode)? → Push it up\n- New user, no data anywhere? → Wait for onboarding\n\nThis is what makes the app work seamlessly whether you sign in before or after using it as a guest."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pages/Debug.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "🐛 Debug Page (Dev Only)",
      "description": "Visit /debug in the app to see:\n- Your current auth session\n- Raw localStorage data\n- App state dump\n\nUseful when something is broken and you need to see exactly what data the app has. Not visible to regular users."
    }
  ]
}